I'll start by exploring the workspace and understanding the data. Let me first list the files to see what's available.

```json
{
  "tool": "list_files",
  "args": {}
}
```

Now let me examine the data file to understand its structure and content.

```json
{
  "tool": "read_file",
  "args": {
    "path": "data/load_15min.csv"
  }
}
```

Now let me run this script to understand the data better.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "cd code && python analyze_data.py"
  }
}
```

Now let me run this script to understand the pattern of missing values.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "cd code && python check_missing_patterns.py"
  }
}
```

Now let me run this visualization script.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "cd code && python visualize_data.py"
  }
}
```

Now let me run the forecasting model script.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "cd code && python forecast_model.py"
  }
}
```

Now let me run the reliability analysis script.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "cd code && python reliability_analysis.py"
  }
}
```

Now let me check if all the required figures are in the report/images directory and verify the report structure.

```json
{
  "tool": "list_files",
  "args": {}
}
```

Perfect! All the required files are present. The report is complete with all necessary figures and analysis. Let me do a final check to ensure the report references all the images correctly by reading a portion of it.

```json
{
  "tool": "read_file",
  "args": {
    "path": "report/report.md"
  }
}
```
